BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Congregation Beth Israel
UID:1404@bethisraelnc.org
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230709T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230709T180000
DTSTAMP:20230703T140847Z
URL:https://bethisraelnc.org/events/cbi-womens-group/
SUMMARY:CBI Women's Group
DESCRIPTION:Our discussion leader\, CBI member Doris Gordon\, has prepared 
 a thought-provoking program about  "Tough Transitions" for women.\n\nDori
 s writes:\n\nLife is in the transitions\; change is the reality of living.
  Life has disruptions\; no one waltzes  through untouched by change.  
 Transitions seem to occur more frequently as we age.    \n\nWhat makes 
 some transitions “tough”?  The struggle to turn the corner takes tim
 e and acceptance.  What were the easier changes in your life?  What ar
 e your current transitions? \n\nAre you stuck in the process?\n\nIn this 
 month’s CBI Women’s Group Havurah we will discuss personal transitions
 \, listen to others’ stories and hopefully gain some perspective on wher
 e we are in our journey.\n\nIf you'd like to join us\, please RSVP to Hel
 ene Nathanson:  Club.Havurah@gmail.com
CATEGORIES:Community Event
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Congregation Beth Israel
UID:8@bethisraelnc.org
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York;VALUE=DATE:20230710
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York;VALUE=DATE:20230714
DTSTAMP:20230427T143438Z
URL:https://bethisraelnc.org/events/beringer-artist-retreat/
SUMMARY:Beringer Artist Retreat
DESCRIPTION:FABRIC EXPLORATIONS With Suzie Beringer\n\nHave you always wan
 ted to create on fabric\, but didn’t know where or how to begin? This wo
 rkshop will take away those mysteries and you will see what exciting possi
 bilities designing on fabric can bring.\n\nBeth Israel is excited to annou
 nce Fabric Explorations\, an opportunity to explore and learn with Suzie B
 eringer\, working to combine strong\, simple illustrations and abstraction
 s to be enhanced with accents and textures of lettering\, all on fabric! S
 uzie is a freelance letter artist with over 30 years calligraphic experien
 ce and a degree in Commercial Art. If you’ve worked on fabric before\, y
 ou\nknow how adaptable and forgiving it can be. If you haven’t worked wi
 th fabric\, you will be surprised and delighted in its characteristics as 
 a substrate. Strong layout and design will go a long way and whether you a
 re familiar with lettering or not\, the enhancements we learn will surely 
 add an element of depth to your explorations!\n\nA good quality muslin act
 s as a tightly knit canvas\, priming itself with each layer. Using this as
  our base\, the focus on this workshop will be on surface design. Suzie wi
 ll guide us in preparing an effective design whether pictorial or abstract
 . Calligraphic experience is not necessary\, but our works will also be la
 yered with lettering as we learn to balance with the colors and movement i
 n our layouts while adding a delicate sense of depth and texture. Letterin
 g can range from your own journaling script\, to a simple mono line\, a te
 xtured effect or any other hand you may want to incorporate!\n\nSuzie will
  share with you many different finished samples that were done on fabric t
 o help inspire you. This workshop will enable you to dive in with confiden
 ce and walk away with enough tools in your pocket to continue that play.\n
 \nSuzie Beringer is a lettering artist who makes her home in the Pacific N
 orthwest. With a degree in commercial art with a life-time passion for cal
 ligraphy\, she is constantly exploring new  possibilities and pushing her
 self creatively. Her work has been published in Letter Arts Review as well
  as other publications. As a teacher she loves to share her passion for ma
 rk making and design with others. As an artist Suzie loves the challenge a
 nd discovery that lettering on different surfaces brings. It has been said
 \, that if something around her doesn’t move quickly enough it may end u
 p with letters on it! You can see more of her work on Instagram: penstroke
 designstudio.\nWorkshop Details\nDATES: Monday\, July 10—Thursday\, July
  13\, 2023 • 9:30am—4:30pm\n\nREGISTRATION: Early Bird registration by
  May 1 \, 2023: $375 (this includes supplies fee). Registration fee from M
 ay 30 to June 30 is $425. Mail check payable to:\nCongregation Beth Israel
  (CBI)\n229 Murdock Ave.\nAsheville\, NC 28804\nPlease include Name\, addr
 ess\, email\, cell phone. OR\, follow this handy link for online payment.
 \n\nFor registration questions\, call the CBI office 828-252-0660\, or ema
 il admin@bethisraelnc.org.\n\nA vegetarian lunch will be provided daily. (
 No meat can be brought into synagogue). Coffee\, tea\, and water are provi
 ded throughout each day. This workshop is limited to 20 participants.\n\nC
 ANCELLATION POLICY: Cancellations made prior to May 15 are refundable\, le
 ss a $36 administrative charge. Cancellations made up until June 15th are 
 eligible for a 50% refund. Cancellations made after June 15th are non-ref
 undable\, however the registration can be transferred to a donation to the
  synagogue.\n\nFor questions regarding this workshop\, please call organiz
 er\, Sally Gooze 828-772-0222.
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bethisraelnc.org/wp-content/uploads/2023
 /04/Beringer.jpg
CATEGORIES:Community Event
END:VEVENT
